1. Kubernetes Storage:
    - In Kubernetes, containers are ephemeral — if a Pod dies, its local filesystem is usually lost.
    - To store data permanently (databases, uploads, logs, etc.), Kubernetes provides a storage system built around:
        PersistentVolume (PV)
        PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)
        StorageClass
    - Think of them like this:
        Concept	        Real-world analogy
        PV	            Actual hard disk/storage
        PVC	            Request form for storage
        StorageClass	Storage type/provider template

2. PersistentVolume (PV)
    - A PersistentVolume is a piece of storage available in the Kubernetes cluster.
    - It can come from:
        AWS EBS
        Azure Disk
        GCP Persistent Disk
        NFS
        Ceph
        Local disk
        etc.
    - A PV exists independently of Pods.
    - Example:
        apiVersion: v1
        kind: PersistentVolume
        metadata:
            name: my-pv
        spec:
            capacity:
                storage: 5Gi
        accessModes:
            - ReadWriteOnce
        persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain
        hostPath:
            path: /data/my-storage
    - Important Fields:
        - capacity: 
            How much storage is available.
            storage: 5Gi
        - accessModes:
            Defines how Pods can use the volume.
            Mode	            Meaning
            ReadWriteOnce (RWO)	Mounted by one node
            ReadOnlyMany (ROX)	Multiple nodes read-only
            ReadWriteMany (RWX)	Multiple nodes read/write
        - reclaimPolicy:
            What happens after PVC is deleted.
            Policy	Meaning
            Retain	Keep data
            Delete	Delete storage automatically
            Recycle	Old/rarely used

3. PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)
    - A PVC is a request for storage by a user/application.
    - Instead of Pods directly using a PV, they request storage through PVC.
    - Kubernetes then:
        Finds matching PV
        Binds PVC to PV
    - Example:
        apiVersion: v1
        kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
        metadata:
            name: my-pvc
        spec:
            accessModes:
                - ReadWriteOnce
        resources:
            requests:
                storage: 2Gi
    - How PV and PVC Work Together: Pod ---> PVC ---> PV ---> Actual Storage
    - Pod Using PVC:
        apiVersion: v1
        kind: Pod
        metadata:
            name: app-pod
        spec:
            containers:
            - name: app
                image: nginx
            volumeMounts:
            - mountPath: "/usr/share/nginx/html"
                name: my-volume
        volumes:
        - name: my-volume
            persistentVolumeClaim:
                claimName: my-pvc
    - Now data written inside: /usr/share/nginx/html remains even if Pod restarts.
    - Static Provisioning
        When admin manually creates PVs beforehand:
            Admin creates PV
                    ↓
            User creates PVC
                    ↓
            PVC binds to matching PV
    - This is called:
    - Static Provisioning

4. StorageClass:
    - Managing PVs manually becomes painful at scale.
    - StorageClass enables:
    - Dynamic Provisioning
    - Meaning:
        PVC automatically creates storage
        No need to manually create PV
    - Example StorageClass
        apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
        kind: StorageClass
        metadata:
            name: fast-storage
        provisioner: kubernetes.io/aws-ebs
        parameters:
            type: gp3
    - This tells Kubernetes: “When storage is requested, create AWS EBS gp3 disk.”
    - PVC Using StorageClass
        apiVersion: v1
        kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
        metadata:
            name: dynamic-pvc
        spec:
            accessModes:
                - ReadWriteOnce
        storageClassName: fast-storage
        resources:
            requests:
                storage: 10Gi
    - Now Kubernetes:
        Reads StorageClass
        Creates real storage automatically
        Creates PV automatically
        Binds PVC to it
    - Dynamic Provisioning Flow
        Pod
        ↓
        PVC
        ↓
        StorageClass
        ↓
        Dynamic PV Creation
        ↓
        Cloud Storage Created
    - Full Relationship
        StorageClass
            ↓
        Creates PV dynamically
            ↓
        PVC claims storage
            ↓
        Pod mounts PVC